# --- Large / regenerable local artefacts ---
# The three CSVs are meant to be committed (team decision — data lives in the repo),
# but anything ad-hoc you generate while poking at the data locally shouldn't be.
*.tmp.csv
scratch/
notebooks/*-checkpoint.ipynb

# --- NOTE on large files ---
# transactional_banking.csv is ~2.8M rows once it lands. If it's over ~50-100MB,
# GitHub will warn or reject it on push — use Git LFS for it instead of removing
# this line:
#   git lfs track "data/raw/transactional_banking.csv"
# Do NOT silently .gitignore the raw data files — the team agreed all hackathon
# data lives in this repo so Claude Code has full context.
